1
00:00:01,670 --> 00:00:04,040
[♪ opening theme song playing]

2
00:01:31,420 --> 00:01:32,430
[door opens]

3
00:01:32,470 --> 00:01:34,050
[HANA] Hi, I'm back.

4
00:01:34,470 --> 00:01:35,890
[DERA] Welcome home, honey.

5
00:01:35,930 --> 00:01:37,640
Tell me all about your day.

6
00:01:37,680 --> 00:01:39,430
Less chitchat, more eat.

7
00:01:39,470 --> 00:01:40,770
[groans]

8
00:01:40,810 --> 00:01:42,390
Mm? Where's Yuru?

9
00:01:42,440 --> 00:01:43,850
Not here right now.

10
00:01:43,900 --> 00:01:45,940
He went looking for a place
to train.

11
00:01:45,980 --> 00:01:48,110
Ken, Right, and Left
headed out with him.

12
00:01:48,150 --> 00:01:50,780
Huh? And you're not afraid
he's going to run off

13
00:01:50,820 --> 00:01:52,280
or get captured again?

14
00:01:52,320 --> 00:01:54,360
It's cool,
Kotetsu tagged along.

15
00:01:54,410 --> 00:01:56,370
I'm tracking their location.

16
00:01:56,410 --> 00:01:57,990
-[Jiro whines]
-[HANA] Oh.

17
00:01:58,200 --> 00:02:00,500
How was work? Stressful?

18
00:02:00,540 --> 00:02:03,290
The Shaman was a pain
to bury, thanks to his size.

19
00:02:03,330 --> 00:02:06,210
[DERA] Who do you think
killed him? The Kagemoris?

20
00:02:06,250 --> 00:02:07,500
Meh.

21
00:02:07,710 --> 00:02:10,710
I have no idea who did it
or why they'd even want to.

22
00:02:11,090 --> 00:02:13,680
Well, who wanted you
to bury the body?

23
00:02:13,720 --> 00:02:15,220
A couple of bandits.

24
00:02:15,260 --> 00:02:16,590
And what did they say?

25
00:02:16,640 --> 00:02:17,680
Not much.

26
00:02:17,850 --> 00:02:19,560
Way they tell it,
they dropped by his shop

27
00:02:19,600 --> 00:02:21,140
and found him very dead.

28
00:02:21,180 --> 00:02:23,770
Could be connected to Yuru.
Perfect.

29
00:02:23,810 --> 00:02:25,350
Possible, sure.

30
00:02:25,400 --> 00:02:28,190
I just hope this doesn't mean
more trouble for us.

31
00:02:28,770 --> 00:02:29,980
Mm?

32
00:02:30,110 --> 00:02:31,110
Hold up.

33
00:02:31,150 --> 00:02:32,690
These are the ingredients

34
00:02:32,740 --> 00:02:34,820
I got ready
for hot pot last night.

35
00:02:34,860 --> 00:02:36,070
You guys didn't eat it?

36
00:02:36,120 --> 00:02:38,320
Nah, we figured we'd wait
and have it

37
00:02:38,370 --> 00:02:39,740
whenever you got back.

38
00:02:39,780 --> 00:02:42,160
So instead, we plowed through
some leftovers.

39
00:02:42,200 --> 00:02:43,620
That's nice and all,

40
00:02:43,660 --> 00:02:45,540
but you guys
didn't have to do that.

41
00:02:45,580 --> 00:02:46,630
I know.

42
00:02:47,080 --> 00:02:49,630
Yuru said hot pot's supposed
to be eaten together, though,

43
00:02:49,670 --> 00:02:51,090
like a family.

44
00:02:56,300 --> 00:02:57,340
[refrigerator door closes]

45
00:02:57,550 --> 00:02:59,430
[HANA] Now, I'm just talking
to myself here.

46
00:03:00,010 --> 00:03:03,100
There were some words
carved into the shaman's body.

47
00:03:03,850 --> 00:03:06,390
"On the next full moon,
at the hour of the boar,

48
00:03:06,440 --> 00:03:08,770
come to Fujimurayama
warehouse one.

49
00:03:11,270 --> 00:03:12,570
I have your fake sister

50
00:03:12,610 --> 00:03:14,490
and a child
from the village with me."

51
00:03:14,530 --> 00:03:16,740
The note was addressed to Yuru.

52
00:03:16,780 --> 00:03:18,870
The bandits told me
I shouldn't tell either of you

53
00:03:18,910 --> 00:03:19,910
about the message,

54
00:03:20,030 --> 00:03:21,990
so I'm definitely
not doing that now.

55
00:03:22,280 --> 00:03:23,540
[Dera sighs]

56
00:03:23,830 --> 00:03:24,910
[Hana sighs]

57
00:03:25,120 --> 00:03:27,170
Whoever wrote it
is in on this mess.

58
00:03:27,210 --> 00:03:29,670
They might even know
where Yuru's parents are.

59
00:03:31,540 --> 00:03:32,750
I doubt it.

60
00:03:32,840 --> 00:03:34,590
If they had his mom and dad,

61
00:03:34,630 --> 00:03:38,470
they'd use them as hostages
to lure Yuru out into the open.

62
00:03:38,840 --> 00:03:41,510
At the very least,
I don't think his parents

63
00:03:41,560 --> 00:03:44,430
are being held by the person
who mutilated the shaman.

64
00:03:44,470 --> 00:03:45,520
[Jiro whines]

65
00:03:45,560 --> 00:03:48,190
That said,
they may have good intel.

66
00:03:48,230 --> 00:03:49,810
This could be interesting.

67
00:03:51,400 --> 00:03:53,730
I'm not sure
that's the word I'd use.

68
00:03:53,980 --> 00:03:56,110
Okay, that's all from me.

69
00:03:56,150 --> 00:03:59,030
I'm wiping my brain
and forgetting I saw anything.

70
00:03:59,070 --> 00:04:01,450
Whatever happens next
is up to you.

71
00:04:01,820 --> 00:04:03,330
[Dera groans]

72
00:04:03,700 --> 00:04:04,950
What a pain in the ass

73
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:06,790
-this is turning out to be.
-[TV beeps]

74
00:04:06,830 --> 00:04:08,540
-[TV chatter]
-So now what?

75
00:04:08,580 --> 00:04:10,670
Wait, when's the hour
of the boar

76
00:04:10,710 --> 00:04:12,040
on the next full moon?

77
00:04:12,090 --> 00:04:14,750
Around 10:00 p.m.
on the 14th of this month.

78
00:04:14,800 --> 00:04:15,960
[NEWSCASTER] In fact, you may...

79
00:04:16,010 --> 00:04:18,130
For someone
who isn't getting involved,

80
00:04:18,180 --> 00:04:19,550
you sure did your research.

81
00:04:22,970 --> 00:04:25,010
[KEN] I'm not seeing
any place it would be okay

82
00:04:25,060 --> 00:04:26,520
for us to practice archery.

83
00:04:26,560 --> 00:04:27,680
[YURU] Me neither.

84
00:04:28,600 --> 00:04:30,850
There are
way too many people around.

85
00:04:31,350 --> 00:04:34,360
I know. One gust of wind
or a messed-up shot,

86
00:04:34,400 --> 00:04:35,900
and we might hit somebody.

87
00:04:35,940 --> 00:04:38,950
Perhaps Asa's daemons
could swallow us again.

88
00:04:38,990 --> 00:04:40,780
No, thanks. Uh?

89
00:04:41,360 --> 00:04:42,820
[panting]

90
00:04:43,740 --> 00:04:45,990
[YURU] Ken, look!
These fish are huge.

91
00:04:46,040 --> 00:04:47,330
Dinner!

92
00:04:47,370 --> 00:04:48,830
Yuru, are you crazy?

93
00:04:48,870 --> 00:04:51,790
Read the sign.
Fishing isn't allowed!

94
00:04:51,830 --> 00:04:53,040
That's fine.

95
00:04:53,080 --> 00:04:54,800
I can grab one
when it's in the shallows.

96
00:04:54,840 --> 00:04:56,340
It's not about
the method you use.

97
00:04:56,380 --> 00:04:58,970
It's just that I hoped
to find something

98
00:04:59,010 --> 00:05:00,090
for Hana's hot pot.

99
00:05:00,130 --> 00:05:02,050
And it's not about
your motives either.

100
00:05:02,090 --> 00:05:04,300
[grunts] What's with this guy?

101
00:05:04,350 --> 00:05:06,560
He's weirdly nice
for a barbarian.

102
00:05:06,600 --> 00:05:08,520
Why don't people hunt here?

103
00:05:08,560 --> 00:05:11,190
There's plenty of food.
If you know where to look.

104
00:05:11,690 --> 00:05:14,270
Like those birds.
They'd be easy to catch.

105
00:05:14,310 --> 00:05:15,560
Yeah, not a chance.

106
00:05:15,610 --> 00:05:17,520
You can't hunt
everything you see.

107
00:05:17,570 --> 00:05:20,650
Oh, right, Dera did mention
something about licenses.

108
00:05:20,690 --> 00:05:22,660
Exactly, that's the law.

109
00:05:23,030 --> 00:05:25,120
[YURU] It's also odd
that no one walks around

110
00:05:25,160 --> 00:05:26,740
with a bow or a machete.

111
00:05:27,330 --> 00:05:29,950
It's like they're asking
for some bandits to attack them.

112
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:32,500
Look, dude, we've got people
called "police officers"

113
00:05:32,540 --> 00:05:33,670
to defend the public.

114
00:05:34,460 --> 00:05:36,170
This isn't your village,
you know?

115
00:05:36,210 --> 00:05:39,380
Kill somebody, and you'll get
arrested for murder,

116
00:05:39,420 --> 00:05:41,550
even if you think you have
a good reason to do it.

117
00:05:41,590 --> 00:05:43,180
[Yuru exclaims]

118
00:05:43,220 --> 00:05:45,680
[KEN] What? Don't tell me.

119
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:48,060
That was a surprise?

120
00:05:48,850 --> 00:05:51,190
Did no one teach him
the basic dos and don'ts

121
00:05:51,230 --> 00:05:52,940
of living down here?

122
00:05:52,980 --> 00:05:54,020
[gasps]

123
00:05:54,060 --> 00:05:55,900
No normal person
would be caught dead

124
00:05:55,940 --> 00:05:57,900
associating
with Higashi Village.

125
00:05:58,400 --> 00:06:01,690
[KEN] Okay, then it falls on me
to set him straight.

126
00:06:01,740 --> 00:06:03,700
Wait, that makes no sense.

127
00:06:03,740 --> 00:06:05,360
You should be able
to protect yourself

128
00:06:05,410 --> 00:06:07,660
if an enemy is out there
trying to murder you!

129
00:06:07,700 --> 00:06:10,580
[breathes sharply] Sure,
but if you take it too far,

130
00:06:10,620 --> 00:06:12,870
even self-defense
can turn into a crime.

131
00:06:13,370 --> 00:06:14,460
[RIGHT] Huh?

132
00:06:14,500 --> 00:06:15,540
[KOTETSU] Mm?

133
00:06:15,630 --> 00:06:18,420
[RIGHT] Yuru, there be
daemons nearby.

134
00:06:18,460 --> 00:06:20,500
-Are they hostile?
-[RIGHT] I know not.

135
00:06:20,550 --> 00:06:22,720
[YURU] My weapons
aren't tested for battle yet,

136
00:06:22,760 --> 00:06:25,180
so I'd like to avoid
unnecessary conflict.

137
00:06:25,220 --> 00:06:26,380
We should leave.

138
00:06:26,680 --> 00:06:28,350
-Right. As you command.
-[KEN] Uh?

139
00:06:28,390 --> 00:06:30,970
Way to make
the smart call, Yuru!

140
00:06:31,020 --> 00:06:32,230
♪

141
00:06:34,060 --> 00:06:35,690
[panting]

142
00:06:42,780 --> 00:06:44,780
[footsteps]

143
00:06:51,080 --> 00:06:52,950
[LEFT] We're being followed.

144
00:06:53,620 --> 00:06:55,790
And I suspect
they've sensed us as well.

145
00:06:55,830 --> 00:06:57,460
[Ken exclaims]

146
00:06:57,830 --> 00:06:59,170
[YURU] Who is it?

147
00:06:59,210 --> 00:07:01,670
An ally or an enemy?

148
00:07:01,710 --> 00:07:02,960
[dog panting]

149
00:07:05,590 --> 00:07:08,010
[WOMAN] They're heading
to an isolated area.

150
00:07:08,970 --> 00:07:10,640
[MAN] Did they notice us?

151
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:12,930
It took so long to find them.

152
00:07:12,970 --> 00:07:14,980
[WOMAN]
We won't let them get away.

153
00:07:16,100 --> 00:07:19,060
Our pursuers are approaching
quite conspicuously.

154
00:07:19,110 --> 00:07:21,520
So do you think
they're after Yuru?

155
00:07:23,320 --> 00:07:24,490
[YURU] Enough.

156
00:07:27,860 --> 00:07:30,620
We'll take care of this here.
If they are enemies,

157
00:07:30,660 --> 00:07:32,870
I'll be facing them
with an untested bow.

158
00:07:32,910 --> 00:07:35,620
Ken, I might not be able
to protect you at all

159
00:07:35,660 --> 00:07:36,660
in this fight.

160
00:07:36,710 --> 00:07:38,920
[whimpers] I'll try not to die.

161
00:07:38,960 --> 00:07:40,460
They approach.

162
00:07:40,500 --> 00:07:42,380
Let us see who they are.

163
00:07:42,750 --> 00:07:44,170
[dog panting]

164
00:07:51,350 --> 00:07:54,100
[MAN] You're a master
and his daemons, aren't you?

165
00:07:56,940 --> 00:07:58,770
[YURU] They're dressed in black.

166
00:07:58,810 --> 00:08:00,400
Kagemoris?

167
00:08:00,440 --> 00:08:02,560
I don't detect any bloodlust.

168
00:08:02,820 --> 00:08:03,980
Still...

169
00:08:04,320 --> 00:08:06,990
[HANA] What if I changed my mind
and decided to kill you?

170
00:08:07,650 --> 00:08:09,860
It would be too late to escape.

171
00:08:09,910 --> 00:08:11,240
[RIGHT] What do you want?

172
00:08:11,280 --> 00:08:13,950
If I were you,
I'd answer carefully.

173
00:08:13,990 --> 00:08:15,410
[WOMAN] Please relax!

174
00:08:15,450 --> 00:08:16,540
[MAN]
You have the wrong idea!

175
00:08:16,580 --> 00:08:18,420
We mean you no harm.
I swear it!

176
00:08:18,460 --> 00:08:20,630
Here, we'll remove
our disguises.

177
00:08:20,670 --> 00:08:22,420
Uh? Disguises?

178
00:08:22,460 --> 00:08:23,840
[MAN]
We have to accompany

179
00:08:23,880 --> 00:08:26,090
our master on walks,
or else they get harassed

180
00:08:26,130 --> 00:08:27,920
or taken
to the animal control center.

181
00:08:28,470 --> 00:08:30,260
[WOMAN]
So we pretend to be a couple

182
00:08:30,300 --> 00:08:32,550
of regular pet owners
walking their dog.

183
00:08:32,600 --> 00:08:34,260
We steal, um, I mean,

184
00:08:34,310 --> 00:08:37,180
we borrow clothes and wigs
to look like humans.

185
00:08:37,230 --> 00:08:38,430
[Ken gasps]

186
00:08:40,140 --> 00:08:41,480
[dog pants]

187
00:08:44,110 --> 00:08:47,110
This is what we look like
in our natural state.

188
00:08:47,150 --> 00:08:49,400
Holy! For a second there,

189
00:08:49,450 --> 00:08:51,530
I thought you two were
Tenaga-Ashinaga.

190
00:08:51,570 --> 00:08:54,740
No, Yuru,
these are freaking aliens.

191
00:08:54,780 --> 00:08:56,290
[BOTH] We're daemons.

192
00:08:56,330 --> 00:08:58,250
For some reason,
people who can see us

193
00:08:58,290 --> 00:09:00,210
always mistake us for aliens.

194
00:09:00,250 --> 00:09:01,920
I find it extremely rude.

195
00:09:01,960 --> 00:09:04,630
We're obviously
run-of-the-mill daemons.

196
00:09:04,670 --> 00:09:06,960
All right, moving along.

197
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:08,670
What are we supposed
to call you?

198
00:09:08,720 --> 00:09:10,380
-Uh?
-Yes, of course.

199
00:09:10,420 --> 00:09:11,470
[speaking in fantasy language]

200
00:09:11,550 --> 00:09:13,550
-Come again?
-[KEN] An alien language?

201
00:09:13,590 --> 00:09:15,680
Ah...
[speaking in fantasy language]

202
00:09:15,720 --> 00:09:18,180
The human tongue is unable
to pronounce their words.

203
00:09:18,640 --> 00:09:21,100
I understand. Well,
that definitely makes sense.

204
00:09:21,140 --> 00:09:24,520
[KEN] I'm totally staring
at extraterrestrials!

205
00:09:26,610 --> 00:09:28,610
[FEMALE DAEMON]
Long, long ago in Noto,

206
00:09:28,650 --> 00:09:31,650
the two of us were quietly
revered by human beings.

207
00:09:31,700 --> 00:09:34,320
But as the centuries passed,
we were forgotten.

208
00:09:34,370 --> 00:09:36,910
[MALE DAEMON] When the visitors
stopped coming,

209
00:09:36,950 --> 00:09:38,540
well, we both thought

210
00:09:38,580 --> 00:09:41,080
we would wither away
until nothing remained.

211
00:09:41,120 --> 00:09:42,120
Luckily,

212
00:09:42,290 --> 00:09:44,000
-a stray dog fell upon us.
-[dog whines]

213
00:09:45,170 --> 00:09:48,210
[MALE DAEMON] And we entered
into a new contract by accident.

214
00:09:48,250 --> 00:09:51,670
[YURU] What? You're saying
this dog is your master?

215
00:09:51,720 --> 00:09:52,970
-That's right.
-[Ken gasps]

216
00:09:53,130 --> 00:09:55,850
As such, we found ourselves
in a bit of a pickle.

217
00:09:55,890 --> 00:09:57,390
We don't have names.

218
00:09:57,430 --> 00:09:58,640
Can you believe it?

219
00:09:58,680 --> 00:10:00,680
-Daemons serving a canine.
-[Yuru sighs]

220
00:10:00,730 --> 00:10:03,140
You know,
I could introduce you

221
00:10:03,190 --> 00:10:05,900
to somebody who can dissolve
your contract if you want.

222
00:10:05,940 --> 00:10:07,190
Hold your tongue!

223
00:10:07,230 --> 00:10:08,940
Please don't!
We're fine with this!

224
00:10:08,980 --> 00:10:10,490
-[BOTH] No, no, no, no...
-[YURU] Uh, it looks as though

225
00:10:10,530 --> 00:10:12,240
you're way more
than fine with it.

226
00:10:12,280 --> 00:10:14,910
Actually, we're here because
you seem like daemons

227
00:10:14,950 --> 00:10:16,410
we can come to for some advice.

228
00:10:16,450 --> 00:10:18,700
The truth is,
we don't have anyone else

229
00:10:18,740 --> 00:10:21,080
we can discuss
our unique situation with.

230
00:10:21,120 --> 00:10:22,210
What do you say?

231
00:10:22,460 --> 00:10:24,210
Is it possible you'd be willing
to be our friends?

232
00:10:24,250 --> 00:10:25,790
Aye. That's fine.

233
00:10:25,830 --> 00:10:28,340
Provided that you don't bring
any harm to our master.

234
00:10:28,380 --> 00:10:29,800
[KEN] Buddy daemons?

235
00:10:29,840 --> 00:10:32,970
-We would never!
-Wow! Amazing! Then may I ask

236
00:10:33,010 --> 00:10:34,760
what our new best pals
are named?

237
00:10:34,800 --> 00:10:36,550
-We're Right and Left.
-[both gasp]

238
00:10:36,600 --> 00:10:38,470
[FEMALE DAEMON] What? No way!

239
00:10:38,510 --> 00:10:40,260
The daemons
from Higashi Village? [laughs]

240
00:10:40,310 --> 00:10:42,680
We've befriended
two absolute legends!

241
00:10:42,770 --> 00:10:44,640
Please, may we
shake your hands?

242
00:10:44,680 --> 00:10:46,350
I'm so happy to be alive!

243
00:10:46,400 --> 00:10:48,730
It seems like you've got
a pretty cool master as well!

244
00:10:48,770 --> 00:10:50,270
What's going on?

245
00:10:50,320 --> 00:10:51,400
[Kotetsu groans]

246
00:10:51,650 --> 00:10:54,200
Hey, uh, think you could
put your clothes back on?

247
00:10:54,240 --> 00:10:56,110
It's kind of rude
to stand there naked.

248
00:10:56,160 --> 00:10:58,490
-[female daemon gasps]
-[MALE DAEMON] Excuse us.

249
00:10:59,950 --> 00:11:01,160
[YURU] Come to think of it.

250
00:11:01,200 --> 00:11:04,500
Many daemons cover up,
even Tenaga-Ashinaga.

251
00:11:04,540 --> 00:11:06,750
[KEN] At least they had
the barest amount

252
00:11:06,790 --> 00:11:08,420
of social decency.

253
00:11:09,500 --> 00:11:10,750
[YURU] Mm?

254
00:11:12,510 --> 00:11:14,050
[dog panting]

255
00:11:15,590 --> 00:11:17,050
Hmm.

256
00:11:18,050 --> 00:11:19,390
-[RIGHT] Huh?
-[LEFT] Hm?

257
00:11:19,430 --> 00:11:20,890
[wind blowing]

258
00:11:21,930 --> 00:11:23,560
'Tis your lucky day.

259
00:11:23,600 --> 00:11:26,140
-We have more friends coming.
-[FEMALE DAEMON] What?

260
00:11:26,190 --> 00:11:31,190
[OSHIRASAMA]
Oh, divine guardians...

261
00:11:33,650 --> 00:11:36,110
[Ken screams]

262
00:11:37,360 --> 00:11:38,820
I found you.

263
00:11:39,370 --> 00:11:40,990
Ah, Oshirasama.

264
00:11:41,030 --> 00:11:42,580
To what do we owe the pleasure?

265
00:11:42,620 --> 00:11:45,330
We thought you were residing
out in the countryside.

266
00:11:45,580 --> 00:11:47,000
[FEMALE DAEMON]
Did he say Oshirasama?

267
00:11:47,040 --> 00:11:49,580
-Two legends in one day?
-[male daemon cries]

268
00:11:49,630 --> 00:11:50,920
[MALE DAEMON]
Her splendor is blinding!

269
00:11:50,960 --> 00:11:52,550
Uh? Wait, Danji?

270
00:11:52,590 --> 00:11:54,420
[Danji gasps] Yuru?

271
00:11:54,880 --> 00:11:56,800
Oh, thank the gods.

272
00:11:56,840 --> 00:11:58,180
[thuds]

273
00:11:59,470 --> 00:12:00,470
I made it.

274
00:12:00,510 --> 00:12:02,850
-[Danji grunts]
-Danji. Hey!

275
00:12:03,600 --> 00:12:05,140
Why are you here?

276
00:12:05,520 --> 00:12:08,190
It was awful.
The villagers got massacred!

277
00:12:08,230 --> 00:12:09,650
-[Yuru gasps]
-[Right gasps]

278
00:12:09,690 --> 00:12:11,020
[YURU] Again?

279
00:12:11,520 --> 00:12:14,230
[DANJI] Our home might never
be able to recover.

280
00:12:14,270 --> 00:12:15,730
[YURU] How could this happen?

281
00:12:16,240 --> 00:12:18,030
I'm down the mountain.

282
00:12:18,070 --> 00:12:20,160
There's no point
in attacking them now!

283
00:12:20,410 --> 00:12:23,450
Asa wouldn't have forced
the barrier open again either.

284
00:12:24,870 --> 00:12:27,160
-So that means...
-[Danji sniffles]

285
00:12:27,210 --> 00:12:28,790
[YURU] Who attacked the village?

286
00:12:28,830 --> 00:12:30,960
It had to have been
someone else this time.

287
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:35,090
[DANJI] I think you're right.
I only saw him from a distance,

288
00:12:35,130 --> 00:12:37,090
but it was just one guy.

289
00:12:37,130 --> 00:12:40,340
He killed all of them
with a pair of katanas.

290
00:12:40,590 --> 00:12:42,890
Dozens of adults
were slaughtered.

291
00:12:42,930 --> 00:12:45,810
I think the village
may really be doomed.

292
00:12:46,640 --> 00:12:48,270
My ma told me to run.

293
00:12:48,310 --> 00:12:50,310
To come down here
to protect you.

294
00:12:51,100 --> 00:12:54,270
I ran into Oshirasama
as soon as I got outside.

295
00:12:55,480 --> 00:12:57,190
Whose order did you say it was?

296
00:12:57,240 --> 00:12:58,240
[DANJI] Huh?

297
00:12:58,280 --> 00:13:00,490
It was my mom.

298
00:13:00,530 --> 00:13:02,530
But it's not just her.
I've been worried too--

299
00:13:02,570 --> 00:13:03,700
-[YURU] Wait.
-[Danji gasps]

300
00:13:03,740 --> 00:13:05,580
Wait, wait, wait, wait.

301
00:13:05,620 --> 00:13:06,950
Before we go any further,

302
00:13:06,990 --> 00:13:09,080
I have one thing
I need to confirm.

303
00:13:11,420 --> 00:13:13,920
Danji, no more lies.

304
00:13:15,040 --> 00:13:16,960
You're not a human, are you?

305
00:13:17,210 --> 00:13:18,550
[Danji breathes shakily]

306
00:13:19,880 --> 00:13:21,300
You're a daemon.

307
00:13:24,760 --> 00:13:26,050
♪

308
00:13:29,810 --> 00:13:30,890
What?

309
00:13:35,570 --> 00:13:37,900
Did I slip up?

310
00:13:38,900 --> 00:13:40,900
[YURU]
You're not casting a shadow.

311
00:13:43,490 --> 00:13:44,990
[Danji exhales]

312
00:13:46,120 --> 00:13:49,250
[YURU] Left and Right,
Kotetsu, Jiro...

313
00:13:49,830 --> 00:13:52,580
every daemon I've met
had one thing in common.

314
00:13:52,620 --> 00:13:54,750
Not one of them cast a shadow.

315
00:13:56,790 --> 00:13:58,920
Everything else down here does.

316
00:13:58,960 --> 00:14:00,420
It's automatic.

317
00:14:00,970 --> 00:14:02,420
But not you,

318
00:14:02,470 --> 00:14:05,050
because daemons
aren't able to, are they?

319
00:14:05,090 --> 00:14:06,850
[Danji breathes shakily]

320
00:14:08,930 --> 00:14:10,350
[YURU] All this time,

321
00:14:11,390 --> 00:14:13,390
you've lied to me, too.

322
00:14:18,520 --> 00:14:20,780
-Yeah?
-Yeah, check it out yourself.

323
00:14:20,820 --> 00:14:22,900
Our bar has the cutest girls
in town!

324
00:14:22,950 --> 00:14:24,070
Uh?

325
00:14:24,110 --> 00:14:26,700
Hey, Jin! Haruo!

326
00:14:27,160 --> 00:14:28,620
It's nice to see you.

327
00:14:28,660 --> 00:14:30,830
So you've been holding up
all right, Aoi?

328
00:14:30,870 --> 00:14:33,080
[AOI] I have,
thanks to you, Jin!

329
00:14:33,120 --> 00:14:34,580
That stalker...

330
00:14:34,620 --> 00:14:36,500
Haven't caught a glimpse of him
since that night!

331
00:14:36,920 --> 00:14:38,210
Well, that's good to hear.

332
00:14:38,250 --> 00:14:41,460
He was such a creeper.
How did you make him stop?

333
00:14:41,510 --> 00:14:43,550
Did you beat him up
or something?

334
00:14:44,010 --> 00:14:45,550
[JIN] That's not my style.

335
00:14:45,590 --> 00:14:47,760
Let's say he's sleeping
with the fishes.

336
00:14:47,800 --> 00:14:51,520
[Aoi chuckles] Oh, please!
You're such a jokester, Jin!

337
00:14:51,560 --> 00:14:54,390
-Anyway.
-Right. To business.

338
00:14:54,430 --> 00:14:56,060
That Tadera guy showed up.

339
00:14:56,100 --> 00:14:57,360
We brought him to the back,

340
00:14:57,400 --> 00:14:58,570
-like you asked.
-[beeps]

341
00:15:00,230 --> 00:15:02,240
[DERA] Jin, buddy, what gives?

342
00:15:02,280 --> 00:15:04,150
You really think
this is the right way

343
00:15:04,200 --> 00:15:05,200
to treat a guest?

344
00:15:05,740 --> 00:15:08,990
Come on, you tell me to come
to a place with pretty girls.

345
00:15:09,030 --> 00:15:11,410
So why am I not
with all the pretty girls?

346
00:15:11,450 --> 00:15:13,330
We don't serve the likes of you.

347
00:15:14,540 --> 00:15:16,500
Enjoy our finest roast.

348
00:15:17,170 --> 00:15:18,210
[Dera grunts softly]

349
00:15:18,540 --> 00:15:20,460
[JIN] We won't give you
any alcohol,

350
00:15:20,500 --> 00:15:22,090
but how about an apology?

351
00:15:22,460 --> 00:15:23,590
The other day,

352
00:15:23,630 --> 00:15:25,550
some of our agents
were tailing you.

353
00:15:25,590 --> 00:15:28,850
Yep, the old lady's group
and that butterfly.

354
00:15:29,220 --> 00:15:31,680
That decision wasn't made
by the clan proper.

355
00:15:31,720 --> 00:15:33,600
It goes without saying
that Asa didn't know

356
00:15:33,640 --> 00:15:34,810
and wasn't involved.

357
00:15:34,980 --> 00:15:37,390
Some of our members
felt the need to grandstand.

358
00:15:37,730 --> 00:15:39,310
My apologies.

359
00:15:40,020 --> 00:15:42,150
Gotta say,
you're a serious dude.

360
00:15:42,860 --> 00:15:44,820
I have little regard
for the law,

361
00:15:44,860 --> 00:15:47,910
but I do prefer to keep my word
whenever possible.

362
00:15:48,870 --> 00:15:51,830
Enough said.
Consider yourself forgiven.

363
00:15:51,870 --> 00:15:53,240
Now, I assume you're here

364
00:15:53,290 --> 00:15:55,370
because you have information
to share?

365
00:15:55,410 --> 00:15:56,540
Sort of.

366
00:15:56,910 --> 00:15:58,920
More like we've got a problem.

367
00:15:59,630 --> 00:16:00,750
And you're up.

368
00:16:00,790 --> 00:16:02,040
[Jin grunts]

369
00:16:04,130 --> 00:16:05,380
[DANJI] My shadow...

370
00:16:05,720 --> 00:16:07,220
How could I forget?

371
00:16:07,930 --> 00:16:10,300
I am able to make one,
if I want to.

372
00:16:11,930 --> 00:16:14,140
I was just so relieved
to see you again,

373
00:16:14,180 --> 00:16:15,730
it had slipped my mind.

374
00:16:16,270 --> 00:16:18,270
We played together
as little kids.

375
00:16:18,310 --> 00:16:20,350
I don't remember a time
before you.

376
00:16:20,400 --> 00:16:21,520
And now...

377
00:16:22,480 --> 00:16:23,570
there's this.

378
00:16:24,400 --> 00:16:26,110
You had me fooled
for even longer

379
00:16:26,150 --> 00:16:28,030
than the Asa in that cell.

380
00:16:28,490 --> 00:16:29,660
♪

381
00:16:34,450 --> 00:16:38,330
And if you are a daemon,
you must have another half.

382
00:16:39,790 --> 00:16:42,540
[DANJI] You know my other half.
Really well, actually.

383
00:16:42,590 --> 00:16:43,670
[YURU] Uh?

384
00:16:44,710 --> 00:16:46,210
The fake Asa.

385
00:16:47,760 --> 00:16:49,170
That's right.

386
00:16:49,970 --> 00:16:51,930
The girl you called sister
and I

387
00:16:51,970 --> 00:16:53,760
are a pair of child daemons.

388
00:16:54,510 --> 00:16:57,220
And this is my true form.

389
00:16:57,770 --> 00:16:59,480
[Ken gasps]

390
00:17:03,650 --> 00:17:07,230
A little boy and girl,
Zashiki-Warashi.

391
00:17:10,860 --> 00:17:13,200
[GRAND DAUGHTER]
Hello? Hey, Gran!

392
00:17:13,620 --> 00:17:15,120
Where's Oshirasama?

393
00:17:15,280 --> 00:17:17,740
They said they were taking
a trip to Tokyo.

394
00:17:17,790 --> 00:17:20,210
What? That's awesome! Lucky.

395
00:17:20,790 --> 00:17:23,040
And they took a friend
along with them.

396
00:17:23,080 --> 00:17:24,630
Such a kind lad.

397
00:17:24,670 --> 00:17:26,500
Seemed like a Zashiki-Warashi.

398
00:17:26,550 --> 00:17:29,420
Oh, no! What house
were they from?

399
00:17:29,630 --> 00:17:30,970
I couldn't say.

400
00:17:31,010 --> 00:17:33,550
A long time ago, you'd find them
all over the place.

401
00:17:33,590 --> 00:17:36,260
But when they leave a house,
isn't that bad luck?

402
00:17:36,310 --> 00:17:38,850
So does that mean
their house is doomed?

403
00:17:38,890 --> 00:17:41,180
Some old legends
make that claim.

404
00:17:41,770 --> 00:17:43,690
Although, if you were to ask me

405
00:17:43,730 --> 00:17:46,610
it's not them leaving
that causes the home to fall.

406
00:17:46,860 --> 00:17:49,110
I'll bet
it's the other way around.

407
00:17:49,150 --> 00:17:52,200
And when a household begins
to slip into disrepair,

408
00:17:52,240 --> 00:17:55,160
their soft little hearts
just can't take it.

409
00:17:56,120 --> 00:17:59,290
And their masters don't want
to see them sad anymore,

410
00:17:59,330 --> 00:18:02,040
so they'll either
end their contract

411
00:18:02,080 --> 00:18:05,670
or they'll agree to walk away
from the house hand-in-hand.

412
00:18:05,710 --> 00:18:07,420
Ideally.

413
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:10,460
Losing one's home is heavy.

414
00:18:10,510 --> 00:18:13,970
I couldn't put the entire blame
on their bitty shoulders.

415
00:18:15,430 --> 00:18:17,010
[RIGHT] What's this, Yuru?

416
00:18:17,510 --> 00:18:20,100
You only just now noticed
your friend is a daemon?

417
00:18:20,140 --> 00:18:21,520
[YURU] What does that mean?

418
00:18:21,680 --> 00:18:24,190
Oh, yeah, you two were the ones
watching over the village,

419
00:18:24,230 --> 00:18:26,770
so you must've seen
Danji plenty of times!

420
00:18:26,810 --> 00:18:28,400
You knew he was
a daemon all along,

421
00:18:28,440 --> 00:18:29,650
and didn't wanna tell me?

422
00:18:29,940 --> 00:18:31,610
You've both been lying
to me, too?

423
00:18:31,650 --> 00:18:34,700
Hold on, the two of you
played together nearly every day

424
00:18:34,740 --> 00:18:35,950
since you were wee lads!

425
00:18:35,990 --> 00:18:38,280
We assumed you deduced
his true nature

426
00:18:38,330 --> 00:18:40,660
and kept him as your companion
in spite of that.

427
00:18:40,700 --> 00:18:43,160
It never even occurred to us
you might not know

428
00:18:43,200 --> 00:18:45,960
something so fundamental
about your closest friend.

429
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:47,920
-Apologies.
-[YURU] Uh?

430
00:18:48,460 --> 00:18:49,670
I thought...

431
00:18:49,710 --> 00:18:52,630
No, this one is on me, guys.

432
00:18:53,300 --> 00:18:55,220
I'm sorry for doubting you.

433
00:18:55,880 --> 00:18:57,010
I'll say...

434
00:18:57,470 --> 00:18:59,890
we have always wondered
about your other half.

435
00:19:00,140 --> 00:19:03,060
That she was kept in a cell
certainly clarifies things.

436
00:19:03,100 --> 00:19:05,310
[LEFT] We sensed her presence.

437
00:19:05,350 --> 00:19:07,770
Never seeing her
made us concerned.

438
00:19:07,810 --> 00:19:08,980
[footsteps]

439
00:19:09,020 --> 00:19:10,150
[Danji (tsugai) gasps]

440
00:19:10,820 --> 00:19:12,820
Tell me, who is your master?

441
00:19:13,440 --> 00:19:16,110
Who used that fake Asa
to bind me to our village?

442
00:19:16,150 --> 00:19:18,660
Who's the one that ordered you
to follow me around

443
00:19:18,700 --> 00:19:19,700
and act as a spy?

444
00:19:19,740 --> 00:19:21,950
I am not a spy!

445
00:19:21,990 --> 00:19:24,160
I swear to you,
it's not like that.

446
00:19:24,830 --> 00:19:26,750
You will not fool me again.

447
00:19:26,790 --> 00:19:29,710
Back then, you'd always ask me
to take you with me

448
00:19:29,750 --> 00:19:32,420
when I went into the mountains
to hunt. [grunts]

449
00:19:32,460 --> 00:19:35,630
I know why!
You were hoping to kill me!

450
00:19:35,670 --> 00:19:37,090
So you and the rest
of the villagers

451
00:19:37,130 --> 00:19:38,430
could get your hands on Seal!

452
00:19:38,470 --> 00:19:40,220
-I wasn't!
-I'll bet those bandits

453
00:19:40,260 --> 00:19:42,100
were sent by you too,
weren't they?

454
00:19:42,140 --> 00:19:43,140
I wouldn't!

455
00:19:43,180 --> 00:19:45,060
[YURU] So who is your master?

456
00:19:45,100 --> 00:19:47,060
Who's giving you your orders?

457
00:19:47,100 --> 00:19:48,770
Is it Granny Yamaha?

458
00:19:48,810 --> 00:19:50,270
[Danji (tsugai) gasps]

459
00:19:54,780 --> 00:19:56,320
[DANJI (TSUGAI)]
You're wrong.

460
00:19:56,780 --> 00:19:58,530
You know my master.

461
00:19:58,570 --> 00:20:01,530
She's the same woman
I've always called my mom.

462
00:20:01,780 --> 00:20:03,370
[Yuru breathes shakily]

463
00:20:05,830 --> 00:20:07,710
So it's Kyoka?

464
00:20:08,290 --> 00:20:11,670
[DANJI (TSUGAI)] Yes.
Instead of calling her Master,

465
00:20:11,710 --> 00:20:13,630
we were told to call her Mom.

466
00:20:13,670 --> 00:20:15,420
To act the same
as a child would

467
00:20:15,460 --> 00:20:16,760
with their mother.

468
00:20:18,010 --> 00:20:21,550
She gave me a mission,
to watch over you.

469
00:20:22,930 --> 00:20:25,930
My other half,
the one in the cage,

470
00:20:25,970 --> 00:20:27,640
was given a different mission.

471
00:20:27,980 --> 00:20:30,310
Pretend to be Asa

472
00:20:30,350 --> 00:20:32,860
and protect Granny Yamaha
if needed.

473
00:20:34,270 --> 00:20:37,150
So yes, I wanted to follow you
up the mountain.

474
00:20:37,610 --> 00:20:40,820
Because I wanted to protect you
from those bandits.

475
00:20:41,740 --> 00:20:43,910
I know it might be hard
to believe me...

476
00:20:44,580 --> 00:20:46,120
[DANJI]...but it's the truth.

477
00:20:46,160 --> 00:20:47,910
[Yuru breathes shakily]

478
00:20:48,160 --> 00:20:51,420
[YURU] Kyoka too?
Was everyone lying?

479
00:20:52,210 --> 00:20:53,210
That's it.

480
00:20:53,500 --> 00:20:55,840
There's not a soul
in the village I can trust.

481
00:20:56,340 --> 00:20:58,220
They all want me dead.

482
00:20:59,970 --> 00:21:01,470
[Danji breathes uneasily]

483
00:21:03,010 --> 00:21:04,930
[wind blowing]

484
00:21:09,890 --> 00:21:12,060
[Yuru inhales, sighs]

485
00:21:13,650 --> 00:21:15,900
Right, Left? Ken?

486
00:21:15,980 --> 00:21:17,610
I need you to wait here.

487
00:21:18,070 --> 00:21:20,780
I'd like some time
in the mountains by myself.

488
00:21:20,820 --> 00:21:22,530
But if you're all
by your lonesome,

489
00:21:22,570 --> 00:21:24,320
and disaster strikes,
what then?

490
00:21:24,370 --> 00:21:27,910
No, please, Right.
I just need to be alone.

491
00:21:27,950 --> 00:21:29,580
[Right grunts]

492
00:21:29,620 --> 00:21:32,580
If our master bids us to stay,
we will.

493
00:21:32,630 --> 00:21:34,090
We won't argue,

494
00:21:34,130 --> 00:21:37,090
but ask that you not stray far
in your search for solitude.

495
00:21:37,130 --> 00:21:38,510
[Yuru exhales]

496
00:21:41,760 --> 00:21:42,970
[Ken breathes softly]

497
00:21:43,010 --> 00:21:45,220
[footsteps receding]

498
00:21:46,930 --> 00:21:48,640
[dog panting]

499
00:21:54,770 --> 00:21:57,360
[♪ closing theme song playing]

500
00:23:27,870 --> 00:23:30,780
[YURU] Between bandits,
beasts, and nature itself,

501
00:23:31,160 --> 00:23:34,540
the threat of death is
ever present in the mountains.

502
00:23:34,580 --> 00:23:36,410
That made things simple.

503
00:23:36,830 --> 00:23:38,420
Just focus on survival.
